import sys
p = sys.argv[1]
lines = open(p, encoding='utf-8').read().split('\n')
idx = [i for i, l in enumerate(lines) if l.startswith('| 634 |')]
assert len(idx) == 1
lines.insert(idx[0] + 1, "| 635 | 2026-10-23 | **Scales and Key signatures checked by playing every lesson and drill (her 14:46 report: the sharp-order staff tap did not work).** Two QA passes (en/ko, 390 and 900 wide), then fixes. (1) Staff taps (sharp/flat order, find the key): the half step is only ~7 px, so a tap one step off did nothing visible; now there are guide dots on every line and space of the next column, a larger staff, and a message that names the wrong letter ('That is G. Try again.'). (2) Circle of fifths (kf-piece and the four-step finder): F sharp, C sharp and C flat could not be selected (the ring showed C and an empty staff); the three shared slots now follow the key and a second click flips between the twins. (3) Key signature drill in Korean: key names were English on the first question and after the language toggle; now translated when shown. (4) 'What a key signature does' had two nested boxes with two TRY IT badges. (5) PlaceIt named the wrong letter in its miss message (one letter off). (6) The 'Three kinds of minor' blurb said A; the lesson is on D. **For her to decide, not changed:** the right-hand fingering of B flat, E flat and A flat major starts on finger 2 (B flat 2-1-2-3-1-2-3-4, E flat 2-1-2-3-4-1-2-3, A flat 2-3-1-2-3-1-2-3); the common textbook fingerings start differently, so she should confirm the table. Also noted, not fixed: 샵/샤프 both used in Korean, the four mnemonic phrases stay English in Korean, small label overlaps in Korean on the 7-flat keyboard. Patch: sc/patch656.py on the t655 build. |")
open(p, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write('\n'.join(lines)); print('ok')
